WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.366 --> 00:00:00.966 line:84%
One-to-one

2
00:00:00.966 --> 00:00:04.186 line:84%
English lessons can go in wildly different directions.

3
00:00:04.406 --> 00:00:06.700 line:84%
One learner is collecting every animal idiom

4
00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:07.826 line:84%
they can find.

5
00:00:07.846 --> 00:00:10.866 line:84%
Another wants to finally crack the present perfect.

6
00:00:11.086 --> 00:00:13.206 line:84%
A new student is moving to Sydney to study

7
00:00:13.206 --> 00:00:14.306 line:84%
marine biology,

8
00:00:14.366 --> 00:00:17.126 line:84%
and suddenly you're deep into whale song dialects,

9
00:00:17.126 --> 00:00:19.386 line:84%
satellite tags, and Australian slang.

10
00:00:19.606 --> 00:00:20.406 line:84%
And sometimes,

11
00:00:20.406 --> 00:00:23.546 line:84%
you just opened your laptop at a rooftop hostel in Rio,

12
00:00:23.566 --> 00:00:24.900 line:84%
and you've only got three minutes

13
00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:26.133 line:84%
before the next lesson.

14
00:00:26.133 --> 00:00:29.046 line:84%
Atlas lets you turn any of those starting points

15
00:00:29.046 --> 00:00:31.366 line:84%
into rich, specific teaching material

16
00:00:31.366 --> 00:00:33.126 line:84%
built around the learner in front of you

17
00:00:33.126 --> 00:00:33.966 line:84%
in seconds.

18
00:00:33.966 --> 00:00:36.646 line:84%
Create from their work, a language target,

19
00:00:36.646 --> 00:00:39.486 line:84%
a sudden question, something Atlas suggests,

20
00:00:39.486 --> 00:00:42.146 line:84%
or any offbeat idea you wanna explore together.

21
00:00:42.366 --> 00:00:44.146 line:84%
Shape it around the way you teach.

22
00:00:44.166 --> 00:00:46.366 line:84%
Then explore it together through questions,

23
00:00:46.366 --> 00:00:47.886 line:84%
stories, context,

24
00:00:47.886 --> 00:00:50.386 line:84%
different perspectives, and real conversation.

25
00:00:50.606 --> 00:00:52.666 line:84%
And next week, you're not starting over.

26
00:00:52.686 --> 00:00:55.046 line:84%
That expression you stopped to work on last Tuesday

27
00:00:55.046 --> 00:00:58.166 line:84%
is still there, along with all the material you created,

28
00:00:58.166 --> 00:00:59.406 line:84%
what you've learnt about them,

29
00:00:59.406 --> 00:01:01.066 line:84%
and the progress you've made together.

30
00:01:01.206 --> 00:01:03.406 line:84%
Bring back a subject you explored months ago,

31
00:01:03.406 --> 00:01:04.926 line:84%
or get creative with whatever

32
00:01:04.926 --> 00:01:06.586 line:84%
new thing they bring into the lesson.

33
00:01:06.726 --> 00:01:08.646 line:84%
When the material matters to the learner,

34
00:01:08.646 --> 00:01:10.166 line:84%
the conversation goes further,

35
00:01:10.166 --> 00:01:11.233 line:84%
and so does the teaching.

36
00:01:11.233 --> 00:01:12.346 line:84%
Atlas.
